# Only the recipe and its trust anchor are tracked. Everything else in a package
# directory is a downloaded source or a build artifact, and downloads here are
# hundreds of megabytes.
PKGBUILDs/*/*
!PKGBUILDs/*/PKGBUILD
!PKGBUILDs/*/*.key
!PKGBUILDs/*/.SRCINFO
!PKGBUILDs/*/.namcap-allow
!PKGBUILDs/*/upstream
!PKGBUILDs/*/notes
!PKGBUILDs/*/.no-auto-merge

# Files a PKGBUILD references beside itself rather than downloading: pacman
# install hooks, and licence texts that upstream ships outside the tarball.
!PKGBUILDs/*/*.install
!PKGBUILDs/*/*.txt

# Shared helpers, not a package. The rule above is written for package
# directories and would otherwise swallow this one whole.
!PKGBUILDs/lib/*

# Credentials staged for `gh secret set`. They live in GitHub as secrets; a copy
# in the working tree is a convenience for setting them, not something a
# checkout should ever carry. Ignored by prefix so a new one is covered the
# moment it is written, rather than after someone remembers to add it.
.env*

# assembled repository
repo/
*.db
*.db.tar.gz
*.files
*.files.tar.gz
